      Black soldier flies are tropical insects. Most cold-climate operators give up
      after their first overwintering attempt — adults won't mate without sun-equivalent
      light, larvae chill out below 60&nbsp;°F, and outdoor bins freeze. This site
      documents an indoor rig that closes the loop: a quartz worklight as the
      mating trigger, a mesh love cage thermostat-controlled to 28&nbsp;°C, a self-harvest
      bin, and a separate pupation chamber. Built and run from a basement in
      USDA Zone 5b.
